  "description": "The Shift i/O 5 is a powerful All-Mountain / Enduro contender. Built upon our new 4-bar linkage frame with 160mm of rear travel and a Suntour Aion 35mm EVO Boost fork, it features the new Shimano EP-800 MTB-specific mid-motor system, which delivers 250 watts of power, 85 Nm of user-friendly torque, and an internal 504Wh battery for an outstanding integrated look. A Shimano Deore 10-speed 1x transmission keeps things simple while the Kenda Nevegal 2 27.5\" x 2.6\" tires with U-40 double wall rims make you feel like you are on rails around even the loosest terrain. The Tektro 745 4-piston hydraulic brakes, with their powerful braking, will bring it all to a quick stop when needed. The Shift i/O 5 remains one of the most versatile, yet affordable dual-suspension e-MTBs on the market today.\nShift I/O X6 Aluminum frame for Shimano STePS E8000 motor, 160mm travel\nSuntour Aion 35mm EVO 27.5\"x160mm Boost fork\nX-Fusion 02 Pro RL, Trunnion, 225x75mm, Trunnion rear shock\nNew Shimano STePS EP-800, 250 Watts, 85Nm Torque\nDarfon 504Wh internal battery on all frame sizes\nIntegrated speed sensor\nDeore M5120, 10-spd, Shadow Plus rear derailleur\nDeore M4100 10-spd 11-46T cassette & shifter\nSamox forged crankarms, Shimano E7000 34T chainring\nTektro HD-M745 4-piston brakes, 203mm rotors",
